## Ontology validation (Cursor tooling)
Always parse ontology files for correctness after authoring/modifying them. Write any required Python (with
tests) under `/scripts`, using `uv` for dependencies.

**CRITICAL: after ANY modification to a `.ttl` file, validate it immediately** (do not rely on editor lints):
```bash
uv run python scripts/validate_ontology.py src/<modified_file>.ttl   # single file
uv run python scripts/validate_ontology.py                          # all of src/
```
Never skip validation — missing periods, incomplete statements, or malformed RDF cause parse failures that
must be caught at once. (Note: TBox `.ttl` edits are on hold pending RES-27 — see `AGENTS.md`.)
